%N A400895 Number of odd primes p < 2n such that 2n - p is not prime and 4n - p is prime, for n >= 2.
%C A400895 Conjecture: a(n) > 0 for all n > 12 (i.e., for every even integer m > 24, there exists at least one odd prime p < m such that m - p is not prime and 2m - p is prime). Verified for all m <= 10^7.
%C A400895 The only indices n >= 2 with a(n) = 0 are n = 4, 5, 8, 12 (corresponding to even integers m = 8, 10, 16, 24).
%e A400895 For n = 13 (even integer 2n = 26), a(13) = 2 because there are two odd primes p < 26 (namely p = 5 and p = 11) such that 26 - p is not prime (21 and 15) and 52 - p is prime (47 and 41).
%o A400895 (Python)
%o A400895 from sympy import isprime, primerange
%o A400895 def a(n):
%o A400895     return sum(1 for p in primerange(3, 2*n) if not isprime(2*n - p) and isprime(4*n - p))
%o A400895 print([a(n) for n in range(2, 88)])
